{"tutor":{"setspec":[{"name":["Mandarin Random Test"],"lessonname":["Random Drill Practice of Chinese Tones"],"userselect":["false"],"experimentTarget":["tonelearning2"],"stimulusfile":["ChinesetonestimsRandom2019.json"],"shuffleclusters":["0-8"]}],"unit":[{"unitname":["Informed Consent"],"unitinstructions":["<p>Title: An Adaptive Training System for Mandarin Tones Learning Based on Performance Factors\nAnalysis Difficulty Model\n<p>Researchers: <p>Meng Cao, The University of Memphis, Email: mcao@memphis.edu, Phone: 901-281-7348\n<p>Philip Pavlik (faculty advisor), The University of Memphis, Email: ppavlik@memphis.edu, Phone: 901-678-2326\n<p>The content below highlights key information for you to consider when deciding if you want to participate. Please ask the researcher(s) any questions about the study before you make your decision. If you volunteer, you will be one of about 200 people to do so. You will consent by pressing a button at the bottom of the page.\n<p>Key Information for You to Consider\n<p>You are being asked to volunteer for a research study. It is up to you whether you choose to participate or not. There will be no penalty or loss of benefit to which you are otherwise entitled if you choose not to participate or discontinue participation.\n<p>Purpose: The experiment is designed to evaluate the effectiveness of an adaptive training system on tone learning. We will compare it with a non-adaptive training method that selects items randomly for practice.\n<p>Duration: It is expected that your participation will last about 1 hour in one session depending on the time you spend on the tests.\n<p>Requirement: In order to ensure the audio input quality, you are required to wear your headphones when doing the task.\n<p>Procedures and Activities: You will be randomly selected for one of 2 conditions with different training algorithms if you choose to participate. One condition will adjust the difficulty of items according to your performance during the learning session. The other one will select the items randomly for practice. Whatever condition you are in, you first need to do a 48-item pre-test, then a 40 min learning session, a 72-item posttest, and finally answer some survey questions. Please follow the directions and try to do your best. Your posttest performance will correlate with the amount of payment you receive.\n<p>Compensation: You will get a base amount of $7 for the entire session and a bonus of $.05 per correct answer in the posttest. Therefore, your payment will be in a range from $7 to $10.6.\n<p>Risk: The possible risks of this study are minimal. Besides typical risks present from sitting in front of a computer (e.g. eyestrain and auditory fatigue) and possibly boredom, you may experience temporary frustration or confusion. There is only a minimal probability that these risks will occur.\n<p>Benefits: You could acquire the knowledge about Mandarin tones by participating. The results of this research could lead to suggestions for real-world implementation of adaptive tone training.\n<p>For questions regarding the research subjects' rights, the Chair of the Institutional Review Board for the Protection of Human Subjects should be contacted at 901-678-2705 or email irb@memphis.edu.\n<p>All efforts, within the limits allowed by law, will be made to keep the personal information (your Amazon Turk Worker ID) in your research record private but total privacy cannot be promised. We will deidentify your data (remove your ID) after the experiment before storing it on our computers long-term. By participating, you understand and agree that the deidentified data gathered during this study may be used by the University of Memphis and published and/or disclosed by University of Memphis to others outside of University of Memphis. However, no personally identifying information will ever be mentioned in any such publication or dissemination of the research data and/or results\nto other researchers.\n<p>Note that Amazon.com has stated that the MTurk platform is NOT meant to support participant anonymity. MTurk worker IDs are linked to Amazon.com public profiles. Amazon.com may disclose worker information. Additionally, worker information may be available to others (who submit a request) for tax reporting purposes.\n<br><br><p align=\"center\">By clicking this continue button, I consent to the above terms. "]},{"unitname":["Instructions"],"unitinstructions":["First, please put on your headphones. At the beginning of this experiment, you will be presented with the Chinse (Mandarin) 4 tone contours and tone samples for the syllable ma.<br><br> Then you need to finish a pre-test with 48 Mandarin tone trials. In each trial, you need to listen to the sound and make a choice of which tone it belongs to. It doesn't matter if you perform badly on the test. <br><br>You can learn the tones in the learning session of 144 tone stimuli for 40 minutes. There will be feedback for you to learn from.<br><br> After the learning session, there will be a post-test of Mandarin tones similar as the pre-test with 72 tone stimuli.<br><br> Finally, there will be some survey questions.<br><br>When you are ready to begin the pre-test of the experiment, please press the CONTINUE button below.\n        "]},{"unitname":["Samples"],"unitinstructions":[" Here comes a figure showing the pitch contours of the tones. Please pay attention to the differences between the tones. \n        "],"picture":["/resources/images/pitch.jpg"]},{"unitname":["ma1"],"unitinstructions":[" Click the CONTINUE button to hear two examples of tone 1 ma.\n        "],"buttonorder":["fixed"],"deliveryparams":[{"purestudy":["16000"],"readyprompt":["0"],"reviewstudy":["6000"],"correctprompt":["1000"],"drill":["7000"],"timebeforefeedback":["5000"],"correctscore":["0"],"incorrectscore":["0"],"timeuntilaudio":["1000"]}],"buttontrial":["true"],"assessmentsession":[{"conditiontemplatesbygroup":[{"groupnames":["A"],"clustersrepeated":["2"],"templat